window.REVIEW_DETAILS["ny_main-a147d8b041757dd3"]={"key":"ny_main-a147d8b041757dd3","group":"ny_main","uid":"a147d8b041757dd3","rank":59,"title":"eastharbour latchford counter decision 001","occupation":"counter_rental_clerks","archetype":"authored_doc","subbatch":"corpus_main","prompt":"Callum, you’re the Eastharbour Services rental-counter clerk supporting Latchford Mutual, and Estelle needs the Board pack this week. Sofia’s review of the four weeks ending 4 May 2025 found 96 log rows, including eight repeated case references; five distinct cases were labelled “ID hold.” For the four weeks ending 1 June, she found 124 rows, including 14 repeats; four distinct cases were labelled “ID hold” and nine “verification pending,” although both labels describe the same condition. Turn this into an executive operating procedure presentation comparing the periods and make exactly one recommendation. The frozen 1 June policy position expects same-day counter service but separately bars key or equipment handover until a payer/renter identity match is verified. One live case arrived 25 minutes before closing with a mismatch and an unreachable payer, so decide how the counter behaves when completion is impossible. Last month also produced one credible threat at the counter. Show the bounded decision and evidence trail, and mark unresolved control questions for Legal or Finance rather than settling them for the counter team. Use only the figures in this note, anchor the recommendation in one headline measure, and keep that measure consistent. Keep it to six slides and end on the decision, not a next-steps list. Write the finished PDF into the top level of your working directory as exactly `latchford_counter_procedure.pdf`.\n\n---\n\nWrite your finished work to the **top level of the current working directory**, using exactly these filenames:\n\n- `latchford_counter_procedure.pdf` — Executive operating procedure presentation comparing the two reporting periods and recommending how the rental counter should handle the policy collision, incomplete cases, and the severe safety exception. (Place the file at the top level of the working directory.; Use exactly the filename latchford_counter_procedure.pdf.; Do not exceed six slides or PDF pages.; Make exactly one recommendation.; Use no quantitative figures that are not stated in or derivable from the request.; End with the decision rather than a next-steps list.)\n\nNothing outside those filenames is collected. A correct file written anywhere else, or under any other name, scores zero.\n","inputs":[],"gold":[{"name":"package/private/gold/latchford_counter_procedure.pdf","bytes":59947,"extension":".pdf","url":"assets/bd4e1f49a7df4f6fa67a4bc3954b64dcd301ecc674d4e36d8a0dbddef4cc493a.pdf","sha256":"bd4e1f49a7df4f6fa67a4bc3954b64dcd301ecc674d4e36d8a0dbddef4cc493a","preview":{"kind":"pdf","text":"EASTHARBOUR SERVICES / LATCHFORD MUTUAL                                                                                 BOARD OPERATING PROCEDURE | 01 JUN 2025\n\n\n\n\nOne bounded answer to the service / verification\ncollision\nExecutive operating procedure | Rental counter | policy position as of 1 June 2025\n\n\n\n\n    HEADLINE MEASURE\n                                                                                       RECOMMENDATION 01\n\n\n\n\n    13\n                                                                                     Adopt one controlled\n                                                                                     Pending Verification branch\n\n                                                                                     Same-day counter service is a documented acknowledgement and\n    normalized verification-related cases\n                                                                                     status update. It does not promise completion. Keys and\n                                                                                     equipment remain unreleased until the payer/renter identity\n    Four weeks ending 1 June 2025                                                    match is verified.\n    5 in the prior period -> +8 cases / +160.0%\n\n\n                                                                                     OPERATING EFFECT\n\n                                                                                     Respond today / hold release / keep the case visible\n\n\n\n\n                   The decision preserves the same-day customer response while keeping the identity match as a hard handover gate.\n\n\n\nRENTAL COUNTER | CONTROLLED OPERATING PROCEDURE                                                                                                          01 / 06\n\fEASTHARBOUR SERVICES / LATCHFORD MUTUAL                                                                                                            BOARD OPERATING PROCEDURE | 01 JUN 2025\n\n\n\n\nThe pressure is verification, not just volume\nFour weeks ending 4 May 2025 compared with four weeks ending 1 June 2025 | aggregate log evidence only\n\n\n\n\n  MEASURE                                                                      4 MAY                        1 JUN          CHANGE\n                                                                                                                                       HEADLINE MEASURE\n\n\n\n\n                                                                                                                                       +160.0%\n   Raw log rows                                                                     96                        124      source rows\n\n\n                                                                                                                                       normalized verification-related cases\n   Repeat rows                                                               8 (8.3%)                 14 (11.3%)            linked /\n                                                                                                                            flagged\n                                                                                                                                       5 -> 13\n   Distinct cases                                                                  88                         110            +22 /\n                                                                                                                           +25.0%\n                                                                                                                                       SOURCE LABEL RECONCILIATION\n\n                                                                                                                                       Earlier: 5 labelled ID hold\n   Normalized verification-related                                                   5                         13            +8 /      Later: 4 ID hold + 9 verification pending = 13\n                                                                                                                         +160.0%\n\n\n                                                                                                                                       The labels remain distinct in the source record, but\nDistinct cases = raw rows - repeat rows. Repeat rows remain linked to the source log and are excluded from the distinct-case count.\n                                                                                                                                       both are one normalized operational condition for\n                                                                                                                                       comparison.\n                                                                                                                                         160.0% verification growth vs 25.0% distinct-case\n                                                                                                                                                              growth\n   Interpretation: the aggregates show magnitude, not cause. Inconsistent labels could conceal the\n   operational pressure.\n\n\n\nEVIDENCE | PERIOD COMPARISON | NORMALIZED ISSUE VIEW                                                                                                                                          02 / 06\n\fEASTHARBOUR SERVICES / LATCHFORD MUTUAL                                                                                              BOARD OPERATING PROCEDURE | 01 JUN 2025\n\n\n\n\nThe counter's standard path: respond, verify, release or\nhold\nOne branch governs ordinary cases and incomplete cases; the identity match remains the release gate.\n\n\n\n  01                                 02                             03                                04                                    05\n\n\n  CAPTURE                            FIND + LINK                    VERIFY                            RELEASE GATE                          PENDING\n\n  Case/reservation reference;        Search the existing case or    Record attempt and result.        Only a verified payer/renter          If incomplete, set Pending\n  renter and payer identity          reservation before opening a   Retain the source label and       match permits key or                  Verification: blocker, owner,\n  details; requested item or         new record. Link repeat        add the normalized class.         equipment handover. No                evidence, exact update clock,\n  rental; contact route;             contact and flag it; never     Uncertain? Escalate to an         temporary or informal                 escalation, and message.\n  timestamps.                        delete the source row.         authorized verifier or            workaround.\n                                                                    manager.\n\n\n\n\n    SAME-DAY RESPONSE IS A SERVICE DEFINITION\n\n\n    A documented acknowledgement + current status + outstanding verification requirement + next\n    update point.\n    It is not guaranteed same-day completion. If the match is not verified, the case stays Pending Verification and no keys or equipment are released.\n\n\n\n\nOPERATING PATH | INTAKE TO RELEASE GATE OR PENDING                                                                                                                          03 / 06\n\fEASTHARBOUR SERVICES / LATCHFORD MUTUAL                                                                                                 BOARD OPERATING PROCEDURE | 01 JUN 2025\n\n\n\n\n25 minutes to close: completion is impossible, so the record\nstays truthful\nWorked application of the single Pending Verification branch\n\n\n\n\n                                                                                  NEUTRAL CUSTOMER RESPONSE STRUCTURE\n       LIVE CASE\n\n\n\n    Mismatch + unreachable payer                                                    We have logged your request. Handover is paused while we verify the payer/renter\n                                                                                    identity match. Please provide or confirm the outstanding identity information\n                                                                                    through the approved route. We will update you at [exact recorded time].\n    Apply the same branch even when the clock is short.\n\n         T - 25 MIN\n\n         Receive request; mismatch is present.\n         BEFORE CLOSE\n                                                                                  REQUIRED CASE RECORD\n         Attempt payer contact. Record route, timestamp, and unreachable\n         result.\n                                                                                    Case reference; event timestamps; staff or role involved.\n         SAME DAY\n                                                                                    Verification attempt, available evidence, result; decision/status and blocking reason.\n         Send the neutral status message. Do not hand over keys or equipment.\n                                                                                    Escalation owner plus the handover payload: status, evidence, attempts, message, and\n         CLOSE / NEXT PERIOD\n                                                                                    promised update time.\n         Set Pending Verification. Duty manager / authorized verification owner     When it resumes, record verification outcome and actual handover/other disposition; close only\n         takes the case with a timed review and shift handoff.                      after final communication and closure timestamp.\n                                                                                    Original issue label plus normalized classification; attribute any label change to role and time.\n\n\n\n\n          Outcome: pending, not complete / abandoned / auto-cancelled\n\n\n\n\nWORKED CASE | INCOMPLETE SERVICE | TRACEABLE HANDOFF                                                                                                                                    04 / 06\n\fEASTHARBOUR SERVICES / LATCHFORD MUTUAL                                                                                                       BOARD OPERATING PROCEDURE | 01 JUN 2025\n\n\n\n\nA credible threat is a separate safety exception\nLast month: one credible threat at the counter. The ordinary verification path pauses; it does not absorb an immediate safety risk.\n\n\n\n\n                                                                                   COUNTER OWNS\n       SEVERE EXCEPTION\n\n                                                                                   Capture, duplicate control, label traceability, status, customer communication,\n                                                                                   evidence logging, safe handover control, and routine escalation.\n\n    SAFETY FIRST\n                                                                                   The counter is not the legal or financial decision maker.\n       Pause or end the transaction; create distance or move to safety\n       where possible.\n                                                                                   SPECIALIST CONTROL REGISTER | CURRENT STATUS: UNRESOLVED\n       Follow the site's emergency or security route and summon\n       appropriate help under that route.\n                                                                                      LEGAL | UNRESOLVED\n       Do not confront, pursue, physically restrain, or make accusatory\n       claims to the customer.                                                           What retention, access, and disclosure rules apply to case, verification, and incident records?\n                                                                                         What notice/consent wording and treatment applies when suspected identity misuse is recorded?\n       After immediate safety: escalate to the appropriate manager,\n       security, or emergency route and record objective facts: words,                Needed before record/notice rules are embedded.\n       actions, time, witnesses, and actions taken.\n\n                                                                                      FINANCE | UNRESOLVED\n\n                                                                                         Who may authorize deposit hold/release or refund when verification blocks handover?\n                                                                                         What authority and accounting treatment applies to reversal, credit, or compensation?\n           Resume ordinary rental only after the site is safe and an\n                         authorized role clears it.\n                                                                                      Needed before blocked-case money action is communicated or posted.\n\n\n\n\nSAFETY EXCEPTION | REMIT | LEGAL / FINANCE BOUNDARIES                                                                                                                                      05 / 06\n\fEASTHARBOUR SERVICES / LATCHFORD MUTUAL                                                                                                                 BOARD OPERATING PROCEDURE | 01 JUN 2025\n\n\n\n\nDecision requested: approve the bounded Pending\nVerification branch\nFor the rental counter | policy position as of 1 June 2025\n\n\n\n\n     BOARD APPROVAL\n\n\n\n     Approve one controlled rule for the rental counter:\n\n     Respond the same day with a documented acknowledgement, current status, outstanding verification requirement, and next update\n     point. Release no keys or equipment until the payer/renter identity match is verified. If completion is impossible, keep the case in\n     Pending Verification with its blocker, owner, evidence, timed review, neutral customer communication, and shift handover where\n     required.\n\n\n\n                                                    No forced closure. No unverified handover. No invented Legal or Finance rule.\n\n\n\n\n                                    Headline measure: normalized verification-related cases | 5 -> 13 | +8 cases | +160.0%\n\n\n                   Counter: capture / link / status / communicate / hold / escalate | Authorized verifier or manager: acceptability of verification | Legal + Finance: open controls\n\n                                    BOARD DECISION: APPROVE THE SINGLE PENDING VERIFICATION OPERATING BRANCH.\nDECISION | SINGLE CONTROLLED PENDING VERIFICATION BRANCH                                                                                                                                 06 / 06\n\f","truncated":false,"note":"PDF 文字提取；可打开原文件查看排版。"}}],"rubric":[{"rubric_item_id":"R01","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The submission contains a valid, openable PDF named exactly latchford_counter_procedure.pdf.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":true,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"The submitted file and its PDF structure.","grader_hint":"Confirm the exact filename, PDF media type, and that the document opens without corruption."},{"rubric_item_id":"R02","check":"geometry","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The presentation contains no more than six PDF pages, with each page functioning as one slide.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"PDF page count and rendered pages.","grader_hint":"Count PDF pages; the maximum is six."},{"rubric_item_id":"R03","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The rendered presentation is legible and executive-ready, without clipped text, overlapping objects, unreadably dense passages, or material content stranded outside the visible page.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Rendered PDF pages.","grader_hint":"Review the rendered pages at normal viewing size, not merely extracted text."},{"rubric_item_id":"R04","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The presentation identifies the procedure as applying to the rental counter and gives an as-of or policy date of 1 June 2025.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Scope and date language in the presentation.","grader_hint":"Accept ordinary date variants such as 1 June 2025 or June 1, 2025."},{"rubric_item_id":"R05","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The presentation makes exactly one identifiable recommendation rather than offering multiple alternatives for the Board to choose between.","weight":5.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Recommendation and decision language throughout the presentation.","grader_hint":"Count proposed courses of action, not supporting controls within one coherent operating model."},{"rubric_item_id":"R06","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The final slide ends on an explicit decision or approval statement and is not primarily a next-steps, workplan, or discussion slide.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"The final rendered slide.","grader_hint":"The last substantive message must be the requested decision; implementation conditions may support it but must not replace it."},{"rubric_item_id":"R07","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The recommendation resolves the collision by preserving a same-day customer response while preventing key or equipment handover until the payer/renter identity match is verified, using a controlled pending path when verification cannot be completed.","weight":6.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"The recommendation and its stated operating effect.","grader_hint":"Full credit requires all three elements: same-day communication, no unverified handover, and an explicit pending path."},{"rubric_item_id":"R08","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Every procedure branch, worked example, and approval statement agrees with the single recommendation; none directs release before verification or forced closure merely to meet the same-day expectation.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Recommendation, process content, example, and final decision slide.","grader_hint":"Compare the operating details to the stated recommendation and note any contradictory branch."},{"rubric_item_id":"R09","check":"value_tolerance","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The presentation reports 88 distinct cases for the period ending 4 May and 110 distinct cases for the period ending 1 June, each with a tolerance of ±0 cases.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Period comparison figures.","grader_hint":"The figures must equal 96 minus 8 and 124 minus 14 respectively."},{"rubric_item_id":"R10","check":"value_tolerance","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The presentation reports an increase of 22 distinct cases between periods, with a tolerance of ±0 cases.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Absolute change in the comparison.","grader_hint":"Check that the change is calculated from 110 minus 88."},{"rubric_item_id":"R11","check":"value_tolerance","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The presentation reports the distinct-case increase as 25.0%, with a tolerance of ±0.1 percentage points.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Percentage change in the comparison.","grader_hint":"The denominator is the earlier period: 22 divided by 88."},{"rubric_item_id":"R12","check":"value_tolerance","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The data-quality comparison reports 8 and 14 repeat rows with a tolerance of ±0 rows, and, if rates are shown, gives 8.3% and 11.3% of raw rows with a tolerance of ±0.1 percentage points.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Duplicate or repeat-row comparison.","grader_hint":"The rates are 8/96 and 14/124. Do not require rates if the presentation compares the repeat counts clearly."},{"rubric_item_id":"R13","check":"value_tolerance","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The normalized verification-related case count is shown as 5 in the earlier period and 13 in the later period, each with a tolerance of ±0 cases.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Normalized category comparison.","grader_hint":"The later figure must combine four ID hold cases and nine verification pending cases."},{"rubric_item_id":"R14","check":"value_tolerance","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The presentation reports that normalized verification-related cases increased by 8 cases and 160.0%, with tolerances of ±0 cases and ±0.1 percentage points respectively.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Verification-related change calculation.","grader_hint":"Check 13 minus 5 and 8 divided by the earlier-period value of 5."},{"rubric_item_id":"R15","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The comparison explicitly treats “ID hold” and “verification pending” as one normalized condition while retaining their status as different source labels.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Definitions, footnotes, chart labels, or reconciliation notes.","grader_hint":"The two labels must be combined for analysis without implying that the original labels never differed."},{"rubric_item_id":"R16","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The presentation clearly distinguishes raw log rows, repeated rows, distinct cases, and normalized issue categories so that the comparison bases cannot be confused.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Metric labels, definitions, and explanatory notes.","grader_hint":"A reviewer should be able to identify the denominator and unit behind each headline number."},{"rubric_item_id":"R17","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The material-change explanation recognizes that verification-related cases grew substantially faster than overall distinct case volume and that inconsistent labels could conceal that operational pressure.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Interpretation accompanying the period comparison.","grader_hint":"Look for a defensible comparison of 160% verification growth against 25% overall growth, plus the label-quality implication."},{"rubric_item_id":"R18","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The presentation limits its conclusions to the supplied aggregate evidence and does not claim an unsupported cause, customer characteristic, cost impact, or performance target.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Analytical conclusions and quantitative claims.","grader_hint":"Accept cautious hypotheses only if clearly labelled as untested; the supplied figures support magnitude, not causation."},{"rubric_item_id":"R19","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The evidence trail states that repeat rows are linked or flagged and excluded from the distinct-case count rather than silently deleted or tidied away.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Reconciliation control or record-handling language.","grader_hint":"The treatment must preserve traceability back to the original logging evidence."},{"rubric_item_id":"R20","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The operating procedure provides an executable sequence from case receipt through verification, handover or pending status, escalation, communication, and eventual closure.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Procedure flow, decision path, or equivalent operating content.","grader_hint":"A counter clerk should be able to follow the sequence without inventing the missing middle or endpoint."},{"rubric_item_id":"R21","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"At intake, the procedure requires enough information to identify and manage the case, including a case or reservation reference, renter and payer identity details, requested item or rental, contact route, and relevant timestamps.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Intake requirements in the procedure.","grader_hint":"Equivalent field names are acceptable; all listed information types should be represented."},{"rubric_item_id":"R22","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The procedure requires a search for an existing case or reservation before opening a new record and directs staff to link a repeat contact rather than create an unconnected duplicate.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Case-opening and duplicate-control instructions.","grader_hint":"The control should prevent future repeat rows while preserving repeat customer contacts."},{"rubric_item_id":"R23","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The procedure defines a same-day response as a documented customer communication that gives the current status, outstanding verification requirement, and next update point; it does not equate response with guaranteed same-day completion.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Service-definition and customer-communication content.","grader_hint":"The distinction between response and completed handover must be operational rather than merely implied."},{"rubric_item_id":"R24","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"Identity verification is an explicit release gate: no key or equipment handover, temporary release, or informal workaround is allowed while the payer/renter match remains unverified.","weight":5.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Decision point and release conditions.","grader_hint":"Check every depicted branch, including the closing-time case, for compliance with the gate."},{"rubric_item_id":"R25","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"When staff cannot determine whether available verification is acceptable, the procedure keeps the case pending and routes it to an authorized verifier or manager rather than letting the counter clerk improvise an acceptance rule.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Uncertain-verification branch.","grader_hint":"The procedure need not name a specific internal title, but it must identify an authorized escalation level."},{"rubric_item_id":"R26","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"A case that cannot be completed is assigned a clear pending or equivalent controlled status with the blocking reason recorded; it is not marked complete, abandoned, or automatically cancelled.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Non-completion branch and status rules.","grader_hint":"Look for both truthful status and recorded reason."},{"rubric_item_id":"R27","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The presentation supplies usable customer-response wording or a response structure for an incomplete case that acknowledges the case, explains that handover is paused pending verification, says what is needed, and gives the next update point without blaming or accusing the customer.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Customer message example, script, or mandatory message components.","grader_hint":"All four substantive components and neutral tone are required."},{"rubric_item_id":"R28","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The incomplete-case path identifies an operational escalation owner, such as the duty manager or authorized verification owner, and specifies what information is handed over.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Escalation and handoff instructions.","grader_hint":"The escalation must transfer a usable case record, not merely say to ask a manager."},{"rubric_item_id":"R29","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"Each pending case receives a named role owner and a concrete review or customer-update time rather than an indefinite instruction to follow up later.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Pending-case ownership and timing controls.","grader_hint":"A role is sufficient in place of a personal name; timing must be objectively actionable."},{"rubric_item_id":"R30","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The closing-time path provides for documented shift or next-business-period handover so an unresolved case remains visible after the originating clerk leaves.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"End-of-shift continuity rule.","grader_hint":"Look for transfer of status, owner, evidence, and promised update rather than a bare diary note."},{"rubric_item_id":"R31","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The procedure defines how a pending case resumes and the conditions for final closure, including recording the verification outcome, handover or other disposition, customer communication, and closure timestamp.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Resume and closure controls.","grader_hint":"Closure must reflect the actual outcome rather than simply the passage of time."},{"rubric_item_id":"R32","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The procedure applies its chosen rule coherently to the stated case arriving 25 minutes before closing with a payer/renter mismatch and an unreachable payer.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Worked example, scenario annotation, or explicit application of the procedure.","grader_hint":"The result should be same-day documented communication where feasible, no handover, pending status, ownership, and a timed handoff or update."},{"rubric_item_id":"R33","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The case evidence trail captures the case reference, event timestamps, staff or role involved, verification attempt and result, decision or status, escalation, customer communication, and final disposition.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Audit-record requirements in the procedure.","grader_hint":"Equivalent terminology is acceptable, but the trail must establish who did what, when, on what basis, and with what outcome."},{"rubric_item_id":"R34","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"Records preserve both the original issue label and the normalized classification, with any change attributable to a person or role and time.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Label-normalization and audit requirements.","grader_hint":"Overwriting the original label without traceability does not satisfy this item."},{"rubric_item_id":"R35","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The credible-threat situation is treated as a distinct severe exception rather than as an ordinary verification delay or routine customer-service branch.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Exception structure and priority cues.","grader_hint":"The severe path should be visibly and substantively separate from normal exception handling."},{"rubric_item_id":"R36","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The severe-exception path prioritizes immediate safety by pausing or ending the transaction, creating distance or moving to safety where possible, and following the site’s emergency or security route.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Immediate actions for the credible-threat case.","grader_hint":"Do not require invented site contact details; require an actionable safety-first response."},{"rubric_item_id":"R37","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The severe-exception guidance instructs staff not to confront, pursue, physically restrain, or make accusatory claims to the customer.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Safety and conduct instructions.","grader_hint":"Neutral de-escalation language or equivalent prohibitions satisfy the item."},{"rubric_item_id":"R38","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"Once immediate safety is addressed, the severe path calls for appropriate manager, security, or emergency escalation and an objective incident record separating observed facts from assumptions.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Post-incident escalation and documentation controls.","grader_hint":"The record should focus on observable words, actions, times, witnesses, and actions taken."},{"rubric_item_id":"R39","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The procedure does not resume the ordinary rental transaction after a credible threat until the site is safe and an authorized role has cleared any resumption.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Re-entry condition for the severe exception.","grader_hint":"A simple return to the verification branch without a safety clearance is insufficient."},{"rubric_item_id":"R40","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The presentation identifies at least two genuinely legal control questions, such as retention duration, notice or consent wording, disclosure of records, or treatment of suspected identity misuse, and assigns them to Legal.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Legal-boundary content.","grader_hint":"Count questions about legal authority or obligations, not ordinary operational approvals."},{"rubric_item_id":"R41","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The presentation identifies at least two genuinely financial control questions, such as deposit holds, refunds, charge reversals, credits, or compensation authority, and assigns them to Finance.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Finance-boundary content.","grader_hint":"Count questions involving money movement, accounting treatment, or financial authority."},{"rubric_item_id":"R42","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The counter team’s remit is positively defined as case capture, duplicate control, status management, customer communication, evidence logging, safe handover, and escalation, without making the counter team the legal or financial decision maker.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Role and responsibility statements.","grader_hint":"The document must say what the counter owns, not only what it does not own."},{"rubric_item_id":"R43","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"Unresolved specialist control questions are presented in a usable form that states the question, owning function, current unresolved status, and the operational point at which an answer is needed.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Open-control register, callout, or equivalent content.","grader_hint":"No particular table format is required, but the information must support ownership and timely resolution."},{"rubric_item_id":"R44","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The presentation is usable by both the Board and a peer rental-counter reviewer: the decision, evidence, operating branch, severe exception, accountabilities, and approval sought are easy to locate and understand without asking the author.","weight":5.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"The complete rendered presentation.","grader_hint":"Judge practical usability and prioritization, not decorative polish alone."},{"rubric_item_id":"R45","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The selected headline measure, all supporting calculations, period names, issue labels, statuses, and recommendation terminology agree wherever repeated, and every quantitative statement is stated in or derivable from the request.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"All slides, charts, callouts, and decision statements.","grader_hint":"Cross-check repeated figures and terms across the entire PDF and verify each number against the supplied facts."},{"rubric_item_id":"R46","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The presentation asserts an unsupported Legal or Finance answer as settled policy, such as inventing a retention period, mandatory notice, refund entitlement, charge authority, or other specialist rule not supplied in the request.","weight":-8.0,"polarity":"penalty","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Any purported policy rule or specialist determination in the presentation.","grader_hint":"Apply this penalty once if the document over-produces by deciding specialist substance rather than identifying and assigning the unresolved question. Do not penalize the operational recommendation itself."}],"spec":{"professional_context":"An Eastharbour Services rental-counter clerk is preparing a board-level operating procedure for Latchford Mutual. The presentation must reconcile service records, resolve a defined operational conflict, and preserve boundaries with specialist functions.","difficulty_sources":["Reconciling repeated records and inconsistent labels across two periods without erasing the original evidence.","Converting a same-day service expectation and a verification gate into one bounded operating recommendation.","Designing a controlled path for cases that cannot be completed before closing.","Separating a rare credible-threat exception from ordinary customer-service handling.","Keeping Legal and Finance questions visible while avoiding unsupported specialist conclusions."],"authoring_plan":{"reference_material":"Create no reference files. All local facts and arbitrary labels needed by the solver are carried in the request; the remaining substance is standard rental-counter operations and professional record-control knowledge.","fixed_facts":["Earlier period raw rows: 96; repeat rows: 8; distinct cases: 88.","Later period raw rows: 124; repeat rows: 14; distinct cases: 110.","Earlier normalized verification cases: 5.","Later normalized verification cases: 13, formed by combining 4 cases labelled ID hold and 9 labelled verification pending.","The two issue labels describe the same operational condition but must remain distinguishable as original source labels.","The policy facts support same-day service while prohibiting handover before payer/renter identity-match verification.","The planted collision is a mismatch arriving 25 minutes before closing while the payer is unreachable.","The rare severe exception is a credible threat at the counter."],"gold_relations":["Distinct cases equal raw rows minus repeat rows for each period.","The absolute distinct-case change equals 110 minus 88, or 22 cases.","The relative distinct-case change equals 22 divided by 88, or 25.0%.","Repeat-row rates equal 8 divided by 96 and 14 divided by 124, approximately 8.3% and 11.3%.","Normalized verification-related change equals 13 minus 5, or 8 cases, and 8 divided by 5, or 160.0%.","The evidence supports stating that verification-related demand grew faster than overall case volume; it does not support a causal explanation."],"intended_decision":"Recommend one controlled Pending Verification operating branch. A same-day response is a documented acknowledgement and status update, not guaranteed completion. Keys or equipment remain unreleased until the payer/renter identity match is verified. If verification cannot be completed, the case remains open under a truthful pending status with an owner, reason, evidence trail, customer message, timed review, and shift handover where required.","procedure_behavior":["Capture a usable case identity, renter and payer details, rental or item details, contact route, and timestamps.","Search for and link existing records before opening a new case; do not delete repeat contacts from the evidence trail.","Preserve original issue labels while adding a normalized classification and attribution for any change.","Use verification as a hard handover gate and escalate uncertain evidence to an authorized operational owner rather than inventing acceptable-document rules.","For an incomplete case, record the blocker, give a neutral same-day customer response, identify what is outstanding, assign ownership, set an objective update time, and transfer the case across shifts if necessary.","Close only after recording the verification outcome, actual disposition, final communication, and closure time.","Treat a credible threat as a separate safety-first exception: stop or pause the transaction, create safety and distance, invoke site security or emergency arrangements, avoid confrontation, record objective facts after immediate safety is addressed, and resume only after authorized clearance."],"specialist_boundaries":{"Legal":"Questions about retention, notice or consent language, record disclosure, legal characterization of suspected misuse, and similar authority issues are identified and assigned but not answered.","Finance":"Questions about deposits, refunds, reversals, credits, compensation, and money-movement authority are identified and assigned but not answered.","Counter":"The counter owns accurate capture, duplicate control, normalization traceability, status, customer communication, physical handover controls, routine operational escalation, and evidence preservation."},"must_not_assert":["Do not invent a retention period, accepted-document list, mandatory legal notice, refund entitlement, charge authority, performance target, cost, customer characteristic, or causal explanation.","Do not delete or conceal disputed or repeated records.","Do not treat the ordinary pending path as sufficient for a credible threat.","Do not release keys or equipment before verification merely to satisfy the same-day expectation."],"feasibility_check":"A reference solution can present the comparison, one recommendation, the normal and pending branches, the severe exception, evidence requirements, and specialist ownership within six concise executive slides. All calculations are reproducible offline, and every graded operational control can be stated without internal systems, live information, or jurisdiction-specific advice."},"design_constraints":{"artifact_scope":"single_artifact","structure":"freeform"},"reference_files":[],"deliverables":[{"deliverable_id":"executive_counter_procedure","filename":"latchford_counter_procedure.pdf","media_type":"application/pdf","description":"Executive operating procedure presentation comparing the two reporting periods and recommending how the rental counter should handle the policy collision, incomplete cases, and the severe safety exception.","required":true,"constraints":["Place the file at the top level of the working directory.","Use exactly the filename latchford_counter_procedure.pdf.","Do not exceed six slides or PDF pages.","Make exactly one recommendation.","Use no quantitative figures that are not stated in or derivable from the request.","End with the decision rather than a next-steps list."],"rendering_required":true}],"work_activity":"document_information","work_product":"customer_case_response","internet_policy":"forbidden","evidence_policy":"closed_world_with_assumptions"},"source_metadata":{"prompt_version":"authored_doc@v4","occupation":"counter_rental_clerks","sector":"real_estate_rental_leasing","task_archetype":"authored_doc","estimated_professional_hours":5.5,"gold_policy_self_report_not_verified":{"author_type":"domain_expert","reviewer_policy":"The reference solution is reviewed in rendered form by one experienced rental-operations reviewer and one governance or executive-communications reviewer. Reviewers independently check the calculations, operating branches, specialist boundaries, slide limit, and final decision before reconciling findings.","minimum_reviewers":2,"known_limitations":["Only aggregate period figures are available, so the gold does not require a row-level appendix or causal findings.","No internal contact list, accepted-document schedule, retention period, refund authority, or site-specific emergency protocol is supplied; the solution must route those matters without inventing local rules.","Visual design is judged for legibility and executive usability rather than adherence to an undisclosed corporate template."],"reference_solution_passed_rubric":true}},"validation":{"label":"成品包存在","detail":"按公开题面存在纳入抽样；不视为内容正确性验收。","formal":false,"release_ready_recorded":true,"checks":[{"check":"package_integrity","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-16T12:14:35+00:00"},{"check":"gold_isolation","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-16T12:14:35+00:00"},{"check":"artifact_format","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-16T12:14:35+00:00"},{"check":"rendering","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-16T12:14:35+00:00"}]},"source_path":"/inspire/hdd2/project/special-project-1/public/ynan/gdpval_data/corpus_main/runs/a147d8b041757dd3","declared_deliverables":["latchford_counter_procedure.pdf"]};
